      "ref_key": "grid_smoke_transfer_scheme",
      "topic": "grid_algorithm",
      "value": [
        "1. Region = studs joined without a closed solid wall (spec 6.23.3).",
        "2. Each tick, plume mass into the region's hot layer from heskestad_plume_entrainment (or NFPA 92) at the current interface height, with wall/corner factor of the burning stud.",
        "3. Layer volume V += m_e/rho_g * dt; rho_g = 353/Tg, Tg from mqh_hot_layer_temperature (or energy balance with hk losses).",
        "4. Interface z = h - V/A_region; fill ceiling band (2.0 m to h), then head (1.2-2.0), waist (0.6-1.2), floor (0-0.6). A band is smoke-logged above z.",
        "5. Soot mass += y_s Q/dHc * dt, spread uniformly over V; K = Km * soot/V in every band above z; bands below z keep K of leakage (0 unless mixed).",
        "6. Ceiling-jet front: a stud at radius r gets smoke before the region is uniform after t = r/u_jet (alpert_ceiling_jet); until then use the jet, not the region mean, for detectors and sprinklers.",
        "7. Doors/openings: for each open edge integrate vent_flow_orifice over the slices above the neutral plane; move that mass (and its soot) into the neighbour region's ceiling layer; closed doors use leakage_areas_cvm2.",
        "8. Stairs and shafts: stack_pressure at each landing door; mass moves upward to the ceiling layer of the linked storey.",
        "9. Acceptance: a closed 30 x 30 m room must match yamana_tanaka_layer_height within 25 % for the time to z = 2.0 m (AC9.63)."
